ARM WRC+addrs
"Write-to-read causality with address dependencies. A non-multi-copy-atomic
 behaviour: allowed by ARMv7 (non-MCA), forbidden by ARMv8 (MCA).
 P0 writes x; P1 reads x then (addr-dep) writes y; P2 reads y then (addr-dep)
 reads x. Seeing P1:x=1, P2:y=1 but P2:x=0 means the two writes were not seen
 in the same order by everyone."
{ 0:r1=x; 1:r1=x; 1:r3=y; 2:r1=y; 2:r3=x; }
 P0          | P1            | P2            ;
 MOV r0,#1   | LDR r0,[r1]   | LDR r0,[r1]   ;
 STR r0,[r1] | EOR r2,r0,r0  | EOR r2,r0,r0  ;
            | STR r0,[r3,r2] | LDR r4,[r3,r2];
exists (1:r0=1 /\ 2:r0=1 /\ 2:r4=0)
